        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-qft-dirac-projections": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-qft-qed-gauge-data": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-free-action-equations": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and use the conventions of [[def-qft-qed-gauge-data]]. Let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$ be open, let each $a_a:U\\to\\mathbb R$\nbe a smooth real potential component, and let $\\psi:U\\to\\mathbb C^4$\nbe a smooth commuting spinor. The real gauge parameter is a smooth\n$\\alpha:U\\to\\mathbb R$, and all fields, derivatives and compactly supported\nsmooth variations below are on this same $U$ (including $U=\\mathbb R^4$). Use the symmetrized classical density\n$$\\mathcal L_D=\\frac i2\\{\\bar\\psi\\gamma^aD_a\\psi-(D_a\\bar\\psi)\\gamma^a\\psi\\}-\\mu\\bar\\psi\\psi,\\qquad D_a\\bar\\psi=\\partial_a\\bar\\psi+ig a_a\\bar\\psi.$$\nFor compactly supported smooth variations, its spinor Euler equation is $(i\\gamma^aD_a-\\mu)\\psi=0$ and its adjoint. The density is invariant under the gauge transformation in [[def-qft-qed-gauge-data]]. On solutions,\n$$\\partial_a j^a=0,\\qquad j^a=g\\bar\\psi\\gamma^a\\psi.$$\nIn SI variables the corresponding Hamiltonian density has the sign convention\n$$\\psi^\\dagger\\!\\left[c\\,\\boldsymbol\\alpha\\cdot(-i\\hbar\\nabla-q\\mathbf A)+\\beta mc^2+q\\phi\\right]\\psi.$$\nThese are conditional variational identities for smooth commuting classical fields. They assert no global existence theorem for the coupled field equations, no quantum current product, and no empirical measurement.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
