      {
        "id": "lem-qft-qed-dirac-first-order-constraints",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "physical_scope": null,
        "title": "Finite-mode Dirac first-order constraint reduction",
        "reference": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md#charged-gauge-data-and-si-natural-conventions",
        "design_state": "Assigned QFT-MG01 research interface authored as a conditional mathematical item with exact hypotheses and a complete local proof.",
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-qft-qed-gauge-data"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-qft-qed-gauge-data": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice, the constants in [[def-qft-qed-gauge-data]], $\\hbar>0$, and a finite integer $N\\ge1$. Let the real configuration space be $Q=\\mathbb R^{2N}$ with coordinates $(x_1,y_1,\\ldots,x_N,y_N)$ and let $T^*Q\\cong\\mathbb R^{4N}$ have corresponding real canonical momentum coordinates $(P^x_1,P^y_1,\\ldots,P^x_N,P^y_N)$. On real smooth functions define the canonical Poisson bracket\n$$\\{F,G\\}=\\sum_{j=1}^N\\left(\\frac{\\partial F}{\\partial x_j}\\frac{\\partial G}{\\partial P^x_j}-\\frac{\\partial F}{\\partial P^x_j}\\frac{\\partial G}{\\partial x_j}+\\frac{\\partial F}{\\partial y_j}\\frac{\\partial G}{\\partial P^y_j}-\\frac{\\partial F}{\\partial P^y_j}\\frac{\\partial G}{\\partial y_j}\\right),$$\nand extend it $\\mathbb C$-bilinearly to complex-valued smooth functions on $T^*Q$. Define the complex coordinate notation\n$$z_j=x_j+iy_j,\\qquad \\bar z_j=x_j-iy_j,\\qquad p_j=\\frac{P^x_j-iP^y_j}{2},\\qquad \\bar p_j=\\frac{P^x_j+iP^y_j}{2}.$$\nThese definitions give\n$$\\{z_j,p_k\\}=\\delta_{jk},\\qquad \\{\\bar z_j,\\bar p_k\\}=\\delta_{jk},$$\nwith all other elementary brackets zero; the bracket is extended by bilinearity and the Leibniz rule. The first-order kinetic term $\\frac{i\\hbar}{2}\\sum_j(\\bar z_j\\dot z_j-\\dot{\\bar z}_jz_j)$ gives primary constraints\n$$C_j=p_j-\\frac{i\\hbar}{2}\\bar z_j,\\qquad \\bar C_j=\\bar p_j+\\frac{i\\hbar}{2}z_j.$$\nIn the order $(C_1,\\ldots,C_N,\\bar C_1,\\ldots,\\bar C_N)$ their constraint matrix and inverse are\n$$M=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\hbar I_N\\\\i\\hbar I_N&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad M^{-1}=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-iI_N/\\hbar\\\\iI_N/\\hbar&0\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nHere, “second class” means that the constraint matrix $M_{AB}=\\{\\chi_A,\\chi_B\\}$ is invertible. Thus these constraints are second class. For a real smooth finite-mode Hamiltonian $H\\in C^\\infty(Q;\\mathbb R)$, viewed as independent of the momenta, define the Wirtinger derivative\n$$\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial\\bar z_j}:=\\frac12\\left(\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial x_j}+i\\frac{\\partial H}{\\partial y_j}\\right).$$\nThe Dirac bracket\n$$\\{F,G\\}_D=\\{F,G\\}-\\{F,\\chi_A\\}(M^{-1})_{AB}\\{\\chi_B,G\\}, \\quad \\chi=(C_1,\\ldots,C_N,\\bar C_1,\\ldots,\\bar C_N),$$\nsatisfies $\\{z_j,\\bar z_k\\}_D=-i\\delta_{jk}/\\hbar$ and $\\{z_j,z_k\\}_D=\\{\\bar z_j,\\bar z_k\\}_D=0$. For a real smooth finite-mode Hamiltonian $H(z,\\bar z)$ the reduced equation is $i\\hbar\\dot z_j=\\partial H/\\partial\\bar z_j$. These are ordinary commuting coordinates; they do not derive CAR by canonical quantization.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 6, §6.1",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "Complete author-hosted HTML chapter 6; first-order Dirac kinetic term and charged action."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 book draft, §§36 and 57",
              "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 616-page book draft; Dirac kinetic term and QED coupling. This item states its distinct finite commuting-coordinate reduction explicitly."
            }
          ]
