          "def-qft-photon-transverse-space": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-polar-coordinates-formula-for-lebesgue-measure": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-lorentz-boost-rotation-factorization": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-null-quotient": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. On the future null cone write $p=(\\omega,\\mathbf k)$, $\\omega=|\\mathbf k|$, $\\mathbf k\\ne0$, and use the measure $d\\nu=d^3\\mathbf k/(2\\omega)$. The fiber $p^\\perp/\\mathbb Cp$ has the positive quotient form of [[lem-qft-photon-null-quotient]]. For each proper orthochronous Lorentz transformation $\\Lambda$, the action\n$$[s(p)]\\longmapsto[\\Lambda s(\\Lambda^{-1}p)]$$\nis a unitary representation on the square-integrable quotient sections. It is strongly continuous. Under the unitary identification with $\\mathcal H_T$ given by\n$T_p[\\epsilon]:=\\boldsymbol\\epsilon-(\\mathbf k/\\omega)\\epsilon^0$\nand $u(\\mathbf k)=T_p[s(p)]/\\sqrt{2\\omega}$, as in [[lem-qft-photon-null-quotient]], the free translation representation has phase $e^{i(\\omega a^0-\\mathbf k\\cdot\\mathbf a)}$. Its bosonic Fock lift has joint spectrum the closed future cone\n$$\\overline V_+=\\{(E,\\mathbf P):E\\ge|\\mathbf P|\\},$$\nwith the vacuum at $(0,\\mathbf0)$. The energy is the nonnegative sector multiplier $\\sum_{r=1}^n|\\mathbf k_r|$ with the exact maximal square-integrability domain on each sector and square-summability over sectors. These are mathematical free-field representation statements.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 6, §§6.2.1–6.2.2",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "Complete author-hosted HTML chapter 6; massless photon shell, Lorentz transformations and physical polarizations."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 book draft, §§54–56",
              "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 616-page book draft; photon modes, Lorentz-invariant shell measure and Coulomb gauge."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-qft-photon-local-field-strength",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "physical_scope": null,
        "title": "Local covariant physical field-strength observables",
        "reference": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md#charged-gauge-data-and-si-natural-conventions",
        "design_state": "Assigned QFT-MG01 research interface authored as a conditional mathematical item with exact hypotheses and a complete local proof.",
        "dependency_level": 5,
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "lem-qft-photon-smeared-potential",
          "lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum",
          "lem-qft-scalar-causal-commutator"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-smeared-potential": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-scalar-causal-commutator": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Work in the fixed length coordinates $x=(x^0,\\mathbf x)\\in\\mathbb R^4$ with $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$ and $\\eta(v,w)=-v^0w^0+\\mathbf v\\cdot\\mathbf w$; write $\\partial_a:=\\partial/\\partial x^a$. For subsets $S,T\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$, say they are **spacelike separated** when $\\eta(x-y,x-y)=|\\mathbf x-\\mathbf y|^2-(x^0-y^0)^2>0$ for every $x\\in S$ and $y\\in T$. Let $A_0=0$ and let $A_i$ be the transverse potential operator-valued distribution of [[lem-qft-photon-smeared-potential]]. Set\n$$F_{ab}=\\partial_aA_b-\\partial_bA_a,\\qquad E_i=-\\partial_0A_i,\\qquad B_i=\\epsilon_{irs}\\partial_rA_s,$$\nwhere $\\epsilon_{irs}$ is the totally antisymmetric symbol with $\\epsilon_{123}=1$. In the commutator formulas below, $\\Delta=\\sum_{r=1}^3\\partial_r^2$ is the spatial Laplacian acting on $x-y$.\nFor a real antisymmetric test tensor $h=(h^{ab})$ with $h^{ab}\\in C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb R)$ and $h^{ab}=-h^{ba}$, define\n$$F(h)=\\frac12\\int_{\\mathbb R^4}F_{ab}(x)h^{ab}(x)\\,d^4x =-A_b(\\partial_a h^{ab}).$$\nThe effective test is conserved, $\\partial_b\\partial_a h^{ab}=0$, and $F(h)$ is unchanged by $A_b\\mapsto A_b+\\partial_b\\lambda$ for smooth $\\lambda$. Its one-particle coefficient $g_h$ is the vector $g_j$ of [[lem-qft-photon-smeared-potential]] for $j_i=-\\partial_a h^{ai}$, so $F(h)=a(g_h)+a^\\dagger(g_h)$ on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$.\n\nLet $C_0=-i\\Delta_0$, where $\\Delta_0$ is the massless scalar causal commutator of [[lem-qft-scalar-causal-commutator]]. As distributions in $x-y$,\n$$[E_i(x),E_j(y)]=[B_i(x),B_j(y)] =(-\\delta_{ij}\\Delta+\\partial_i\\partial_j)C_0(x-y),$$\n$$[E_i(x),B_j(y)]=\\epsilon_{jri}\\partial_0\\partial_rC_0(x-y).$$\nEvery right-hand side has support in the closed causal cone. Hence compactly supported tests whose supports are spacelike separated in the stated Minkowski sense give commuting field-strength operators on $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$. The quotient representation of [[lem-qft-photon-covariance-spectrum]] makes these smeared field strengths Lorentz covariant: their on-shell coefficient depends on a polarization class only through $p_a\\epsilon_b-p_b\\epsilon_a$. These conclusions concern gauge-invariant free observables and do not assert locality of the Coulomb potential.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 6, §§6.2.1–6.4",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S6.html",
              "locator": "Complete author-hosted HTML chapter 6; transverse photon field, field strengths, Coulomb gauge and locality."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 book draft, §§54–58",
              "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 616-page book draft; electromagnetic field strength, transverse modes and gauge-invariant observables."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-qft-photon-local-weyl-observables",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "physical_scope": null,
        "title": "Bounded local photon Weyl observable algebra",
        "reference": "research/plan-quantum-field-theory-track.md#charged-gauge-data-and-si-natural-conventions",
        "design_state": "Assigned QFT-MG01 research interface authored as a conditional mathematical item with exact hypotheses and a complete local proof.",
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "thm-rational-box-step-functions-form-a-countable-dense-subset-of-l-p-of-rn",
