        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. For each nonzero $\\mathbf k$, the physical photon fiber is the real plane $n^\\perp$ (or its complexification), where $n=\\mathbf k/|\\mathbf k|$, and therefore has dimension two. Locally in direction space one can choose two continuous orthonormal polarization vectors. There is no continuous real orthonormal polarization frame on all of $S^2$. In the Lorenz auxiliary construction, the four-component subsidiary space modulo its null radical is isometric to this same two-dimensional transverse fiber; four auxiliary components do not represent four positive physical polarizations.",
